WEBVTT

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:06.330
Chapter 5:

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:06.330
Kloden`s Surprise Battle

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.090
So, what do we do? Do we have any plans?

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.560
I do have a rough idea... but I don't have a winning move yet.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.550
About two thousand years ago in Asia, there was a legendary

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.230
military strategist who was a cornerstone in the art of war.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.660
Looks like it's still worthwhile holding public seminars on it.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.650
Maybe...

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.680
I mean that we're so close that we've shown each other our naked bodies and underwear.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.430
Does the famed military strategist from Squad 7 have anything to say?

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.630
Do you have any good plans, sire?

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.290
None at all!

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.930
Alicia.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.730
What's the matter?

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.600
Look over there.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:58.430
What?

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.270
I don't know. Something has been moving there for a while.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.480
Could it be... a spy?

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.420
It's really bad news if that's really a spy.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.700
I got it. I'll go investigate.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:19.710
Hey!

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.980
There might be a spy here.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.070
Spy?!

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.560
He's running away! I have to chase him!

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.380
Really?

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.770
Leave it to me!

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.810
She did it?

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.690
A spy... you mean this thing?

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.090
Oink.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.870
Wait a minute, Rosie!

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.250
It's no joke keeping that around when we're fighting!

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.610
Throw it away now!

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.270
Please calm down!

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.710
What's wrong?

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:10.460
I caught this thing because they said there was a spy behind a clump of bushes.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.660
What a joke! This is the spy they were talking about!

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.390
I'm sorry, Welkin.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.550
Wow! A winged pig!

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.100
This is a rare animal!

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.900
If I let go of him in a place like this, it'll be caught and eaten by somebody!

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.610
Since we saved it by chance...

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:32.320
Besides... it must be painful being all alone...

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.630
It's just one pig. What's wrong with you?

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.870
And what do you mean, <i>we</i> saved it?

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:40.580
Because I ran into an animal trail, I have all these scratches on my body, now!

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.620
Rosie, what did you just say?

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.460
I have scratches all over my body?

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.460
No, before that. What did you run into?

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.910
Huh? An animal trail.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.430
It's overgrown with small branches. It really hurts!

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.300
That's it!

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.550
What do you mean?

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.560
Faldio, I've decided on our battle plan!

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.560
Battle plan?

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.110
What's wrong?

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.820
Alicia, hold onto this for a bit.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.990
What's this?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.100
A fruit or something?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.250
No, it's not a fruit.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.430
Then what is it?

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.310
Longbeard goat droppings.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.540
Oh, just droppings.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:33.870
Droppings?

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.670
No!

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.040
Hey, what are you making me touch?

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:42.430
What do you mean? It's just droppings, what's wrong with it?

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.500
What do you mean, what's wrong?! Apologize to me!

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.650
Oh... Sorry! Sorry!

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.900
<i>Seriously, how thick-headed can he be?</i>

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.780
Listen up.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.210
Beyond that thicket is an animal trail.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.970
It's a natural path made by animals that passed through it and flattened the grass.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.900
Animals such as boars, rabbits, or this winged pig.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:17.940
Once you follow that trail to the end, you should emerge somewhere in the vicinity of the Imperial supply base.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.770
You're saying that we should use that animal trail?

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:23.470
That's right.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:28.170
The main force, with the Edelweiss, will approach from the front and draw the attention of the enemy.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:33.190
In the meantime, another unit will use the trail and attack the enemy from the flank.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:42.300
It makes sense, but it's pretty risky.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:48.960
If the Edelweiss can't hold out before the other unit attacks, we'll lose.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.540
Can we really pull it off?

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.000
We can do it.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.440
Endurance, mobility, armour.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:02.010
If we consider the Edelweiss's strengths, an endurance battle to draw away their attention should be possible.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:10.390
Okay. We, Squad 1, shall go with this plan.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.530
Although we'll only be acting as Squad 7's backup.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:22.070
I got no other choice. I've promised to follow the squad leader's orders.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.200
I have no objections.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.160
The main question is our members' deployment.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:34.750
Because the Edelweiss is needed as the decoy, Welkin and I need to stay in the main force.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:40.040
You're right. Moreover, we need sufficient soldiers to withstand the attack.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.420
Who should I entrust the other unit to?

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.100
Can I count on you, Faldio?

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.560
Of course.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.480
And...

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.160
Alicia.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.440
All right. It's decided!

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.950
Wait! Why does it have to be this way?!

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:03.910
Why?

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:08.330
Faldio can take command and provide support from the back.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:14.290
After Alicia has thought about the battle formation, she'll be able to charge in like a wild boar.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.460
Will she be all right?

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.500
Yes! I trust her.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.970
I'll be fine! I just have to do it!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.050
Looks like she's mad.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.560
Huh? Why?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.720
You're not angry, are you?

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.140
I'm not angry.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.930
Let's go.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.120
All right.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.530
Well then, begin the operation!

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:53.200
It'll be roughly thirty minutes before the other troop reaches the enemy's flank.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.670
We have to withstand the enemy's attack until then!

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.840
Enemy sighted!

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:05.680
What is it?

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.800
The Gallian Army is attacking?

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:13.220
Yes, sir. According to our scout's report, it's a company-sized unit from the Militia.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.090
They don't seem to know their place.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.120
It seems we have been underestimated.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.230
Listen to me! Annihilate every single one of them!

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.210
It's begun. We have to hurry, too.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:45.950
Alicia, has anyone ever told you that you're an interesting girl?

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.800
Lieutenant Landzaat, please refrain from private talk during an operation.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:54.740
Oh, you're calling me Landzaat again. Didn't I tell you to just call me Faldio?

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.560
Understood, Lieutenant Landzaat.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:03.570
You're like a Valkyrur from ancient times.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.670
Please refrain from private talk.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.000
An ordinary man won't be able to approach you.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:09.530
What do you think?

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.770
Please refrain from private talk.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:15.330
Perhaps a lover...

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.510
Please refrain from private talk!

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.040
Do you know what kind of situation we're in?

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.500
Calm down, calm down.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:26.380
Besides, we'll get discovered by the enemy if you shout so loudly.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.630
You're the one who's making me shout!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.800
Sergeant Melchiott!

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.940
You need to keep quiet!

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.140
Now, now...

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:41.480
<i>Be it this person or Welkin, why do I have to be surrounded by weirdos?</i>

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:45.020
W-What?

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.030
Aren't you afraid?

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.120
Oh yes, excuse me. I'm supposed to refrain from private talk.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.700
I'm afraid.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:00.420
Of course, I'm afraid. How can I not be afraid?

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:04.780
But if I think that I'm afraid, I won't be able to fight.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.950
If I stop to think about it, I'll be overcome with fear.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:14.140
That's why I can only move forward now.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:17.230
The only thing I can do now is to be the first to take the fighting pose.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.350
That's something I definitely have to do now.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:37.280
Largo!

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.810
The tank on the front-right has strong firepower!

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:40.750
Do something!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.710
Understood!

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.170
Eat this!

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.760
<i>This is still going to go on for a while.</i>

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:58.260
<i>Can we really hold out against that many enemy soldiers?</i>

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.330
Keep low.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:10.780
There are: one, two, three, four, five... six guards.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.940
We should be able to break through that small amount of people...

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:15.810
Can you do it, Alicia?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:20.580
Alicia.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:27.710
Alicia!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.190
What?! What did you drop inside my clothes?!

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:40.890
Longbeard goat droppings.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:44.310
Stop it! What the hell are you doing, you idiot?!

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:47.740
Huh?

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:51.110
It's just a nut.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.320
Stop being so insensitive at a time like this!

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:56.320
A nervous soldier is weaker than any other soldier.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:01.580
If you get nervous, the people around you will get nervous, too.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:02.240
So...

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.330
Don't worry. Believe in Welkin.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.210
I told you that he's a man who does things when he needs to.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.600
Don't advance in only one direction!

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:27.230
Keep changing your direction in quick
succession, and don't fall in their trap!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.190
Yes, Welkin!

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.780
Will Alicia's unit be all right?

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.680
Yeah, they'll be fine. They'll definitely achieve their objective.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.500
So we have to do our best, too!

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:46.920
Are you saying we can't handle a
single tank and a few infantrymen?

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.170
Explain yourself!

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:51.810
Yes, sir. According to our report, this tank is a
few classes higher than a normal Gallian tank...

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.880
...in terms of mobility, firepower, and all other aspec-

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.880
I don't care about the tank's specs!

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.420
Our enemy is nothing more than a disorderly mob.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.320
Since we are superior in number and have the psychological advantage,

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.980
there is no reason we should be having trouble dealing with them!

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:07.890
We're truly sorry, sir!

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.830
Good, now's our chance.

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:26.250
Let's move.

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:35.380
I'll take the lead. Follow me!

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.180
If we occupy the point in front, we can advance quickly!

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:45.680
Sergeant Melchiott! That's too reckless!

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:49.690
Our obstacle is that sniper at two o'clock.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.640
I'll burst through. Cover me!

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.570
Wait, Alicia. Don't be hasty.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.700
I'll go after counting to three.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.910
Hey, hey, did you hear what I just said?

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.910
One, two...

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:02.860
Three!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:05.700
Ramal, cover us.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:06.540
Yes, sir!

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.330
Are you all right?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.230
Sorry. And thanks!

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:34.770
You're really reckless.

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:36.820
You're not hit, are you?

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.940
Piece of cake!

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:43.820
Reporting, sir!

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:47.630
The Gallian Army is attacking us from the west side of the base!

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.620
What was that?!

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:56.060
They planned to take advantage of our troop's confidence in winning because of our greater numbers?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:59.560
It looks like it will not be easy to quell this disorder.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:10.330
Seriously, how far are you intending on going?

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.250
I'll go as far as my feet take me.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.130
Are you tired already?

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.100
Can you keep up?

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.120
You're the one who said it.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.490
If I keep being taken for a fool, it'll hurt my reputation as a squad leader.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.070
I'll follow you to the end.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.240
Now that's the way.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.540
Alicia! Duck!

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.000
Alicia!

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:39.670
Ramal!

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:41.130
Yes!

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.090
Hang on!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.250
Alicia, are you okay?

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.860
Y-You!

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:01.860
Jaeger!

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:08.320
For someone who's feared as the Empire's Demon, you're in quite an ugly state.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:12.070
Quiet. Why are you here?

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.500
Hey, hey, have you forgotten?

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:16.750
My mission is to watch your back.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:21.380
I'm not in a situation that I can't handle.

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:24.510
Are you blinded by your desire for credit?

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.370
Hey, that's not a very nice thing to say.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:31.220
I'm not forcing you to accept my assistance.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:34.770
But we ought to retreat.

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:39.940
It'll be painful to lose this base, but we can't afford to let our losses escalate.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:43.850
Don't worry about it!

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:47.380
I didn't bring my troops here to fight.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.070
I came to protect you and the ragnite.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.080
I won't make you lose face.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:57.580
Linus.

00:15:58.050 --> 00:15:59.330
We will retreat.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:04.690
Put the transport of the ragnite as your top priority and order the whole army to retreat.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:05.460
Yes, sir!

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:17.380
<i>An ordinary officer would refuse to acknowledge his own mistakes and dig his own grave in the process.</i>

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.180
<i>I expect nothing less from Gregor.</i>

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:26.030
Are you all right, Alicia? Hey!

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:31.720
I'm all right. Ever since I was a child,
my wounds have healed really quickly.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.740
I'll be depending on you to cover me, Lieutenant Landzaat.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:37.340
Just call me Faldio.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.410
But you mustn't be rash.

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:42.830
Don't worry. I'm counting on you, Faldio! {what a slut!}

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:53.640
Reporting in! General Gregor and the ragnite transporting team have retreated safely.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:58.600
Okay, I got it. Let us retreat bit-by-bit, then.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.920
You better leave, too.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.140
Yes, sir! Thank you, sir!

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:06.830
Come to think of it...

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:12.990
With our vast numbers, it's unthinkable that we'd be pushed around by a few amateur soldiers.

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:24.320
Okay, we're the only ones left. Let's retreat.

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.330
Oh man...

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:37.180
A lovely girl like that running around on the battlefield?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.190
Oh, wow. You're good.

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:49.250
Look, our dear enemy is coming.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.360
Rain her with bullets.

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:56.830
They're planning to escape, eh?

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:00.590
Everyone, don't fall behind Alicia.

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.230
Cover her!

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:03.420
Alicia, stop!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.170
Welkin.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:10.750
Welkin, now's the chance to beat them!

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:11.870
It's all right.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.120
This time, our only mission is to occupy this base.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.220
There's no need to chase them.

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:18.860
You're too soft.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:22.630
Letting this opportunity slip by will
only bring danger to us in the future.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:23.440
Am I not mistaken?

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.590
You may be right.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:31.170
But this enemy commander ordered the whole army to retreat when the situation changed.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:35.660
It's dangerous to depend on momentum when facing a commander who gave such a decisive order.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:41.260
Moreover, Squad 7 has to right to command this time around.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:45.310
I cannot put my soldiers in any more danger.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.250
I'm sorry.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:50.090
I understand.

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:52.710
You're quite naive, you know?

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:00.190
<i>Oh? They're not coming after us.</i>

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:04.090
<i>It seems they have a capable commander, after all.</i>

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:06.790
<i>If that girl...</i>

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.400
It can't be...

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:18.980
You see? It's thanks to this pig that our battle plan was a success.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:20.830
We can bring it along from now on, right?

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:24.000
Geez, I'm not going to bother with you anymore.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.460
What name should I give it?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.710
I know! Hans!

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.260
Hans, you say?

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:37.090
Right! It just came to me.

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:39.900
Your name is Hans from now on.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.700
You're not alone anymore.

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:43.690
Is your wound all right?

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:46.130
Yes, I'm okay.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:46.670
Anywa-

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:49.690
As an apology for the Longbeard goat droppings the other day, take these.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:52.940
These nuts are the favourite of winged pigs.

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:57.650
Are you two teasing me? I don't need that.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.410
What's wrong with her?

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:01.620
No idea.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:07.930
<i>She really is an interesting girl.</i>

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:11.860
Pleased to meet you.

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:14.160
I'm Irene Ellet from Radio GBS.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:20.710
Do you know about the upcoming star of the Militia in Squad 7 of the 3rd Regiment, Welkin Gunther?

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.240
What's the secret to his popularity?

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.880
What is your impression of Lieutenant Gunther?

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.420
How do you think it's going to turn out?

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:31.400
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles, Chapter 6.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:33.550
War Correspondent, Hard Struggle!

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:37.490
Radio GBS, judging the world impartially and reporting only the truth.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.950
Chapter 6:

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.950
War Correspondent, Hard Struggle!

00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:39.370
The signals are crackling; we're on the air!
